<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_245349bc-b639-4636-84fe-c4255f70cb10"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref refid="act-2025-004"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Sound NSW
Advisory Board Act 2025</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e5d4eb8f-aca3-4ed8-8a3b-5478be001ca9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_54b4e31a-e3cc-4a0a-a4db-e1fd0507aba8"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on the date of assent to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_66b4fd19-9c85-4ed3-a1b2-835e03019ff7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_495a3baa-bd8b-4e61-bd4e-495bd7230c7c"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_165e49e8-f2ba-451f-ad10-606ba19ef4e9"
id="sec.3-def.Board"><b><i>Board</i></b></defterm>&#8212;see section
5.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_feda6b53-52ff-4d7b-86fd-040d70e7d76d"
id="sec.3-def.chairperson"><b><i>chairperson</i></b></defterm> means the
chairperson of the Board.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_d6f78c40-4a1c-49dc-98be-60db169da15f"
id="sec.3-def.charter"><b><i>charter</i></b></defterm> means a charter issued
by the Minister under section 8.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f93a04cc-13f6-4584-8129-becf03f09819"
id="sec.3-def.deputychairperson"><b><i>deputy chairperson</i></b></defterm>
means the deputy chairperson of the Board.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_8f7bed84-5e7f-463a-b1ce-59384e6e3fbe"
id="sec.3-def.member"><b><i>member</i></b></defterm> means a member of the
Board appointed under section 6.</txt></block></deflist>
</block>
<note type="legtext" guid="_c854f84b-5190-4e46-872d-5354fdb4d5ef"
id="sec.3-note"><heading guid="_e507a166-ccdb-44a9-9f03-2d66c1e6044a"
id="sec.3-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">The <legref refid="act-1987-015" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Interpretation Act
1987</i></name></legref> contains definitions and other provisions that affect
the interpretation and application of this Act.</txt></block></note>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7700dd9f-b0f0-4e8a-ba0f-75a52403d497"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_95802db2-c24b-4fbe-8df0-6dbc141b0124"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Object of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The object of this Act is to assist, promote and
strengthen the contemporary music industry in New South Wales by establishing
the Sound NSW Advisory Board to advise the Minister.</txt></block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dc2e11b7-af37-4c39-ab07-34d7419198dd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_91b9d4b0-bdbe-4c9c-8f1c-ca694feb394c"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Sound NSW Advisory Board</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5a4c0b06-5261-4f6f-8553-ce34ddab1d3f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_1084964e-3b48-4622-92db-0fa0e2248f36"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Establishment of Board</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Sound NSW Advisory Board (the <defterm
type="definition" guid="_3ca5234c-ea45-4885-838e-4044258c6a11"
id="sec.5-def.Board"><b><i>Board</i></b></defterm>) is
established.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_39539a48-52d2-4b10-b3d4-96d5da64ccc9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_fa469075-20e4-41c6-a83e-b39f6513d52a"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Membership of Board</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dc123aad-995d-4730-a7cb-f95c343012ed"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Board must consist of the following members
appointed by the Minister&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_715008ac-01b4-4505-9cc6-cc7562687a39" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a chairperson,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_48fbedfe-e77a-47f2-b7d7-38abd13150b3" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">at least 8, and not more than 11, other
members.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_43deeacb-aa92-4824-b903-215bdcdee067"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The regulations may provide for matters relating
to the members, including eligibility and other requirements for
appointment.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0d85b304-c021-4ddd-9675-46a3c60705fb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may appoint 1 member of the Board as
the deputy chairperson of the Board.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1156b0f2-2dcf-4d3e-a83c-0505359acfcd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Schedule 1 contains provisions relating to the
members of the Board.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_175d2828-17c0-4745-b2f8-5793ca2edd9d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_8bb11a27-f3b5-4989-be66-c7ebb82615db"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Functions of Board</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bae7b3ee-d634-4d6f-9b02-f4d8b69308f4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Board&#8217;s principal function is to
provide advice to the Minister about the contemporary music industry in New
South Wales.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8b40b38f-a0ed-4caa-ba4f-6f0a2523085b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without limiting subsection (1), the
Board&#8217;s functions include the following&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3454522f-2f3d-460b-ab1b-97953413cc88" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to identify issues affecting the contemporary
music industry,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6d3c1213-346e-454c-88a7-ced426f49a3e" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to provide advice to the Minister about
priorities, projects and proposals relating to the contemporary music
industry,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2a696f74-d84e-40dc-91a9-775006c62e3c" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to identify opportunities to improve the
contemporary music industry,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_780b3827-c544-4422-a64c-0029a23e0a8a" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to provide advice to the Minister about matters
relating to the intersection between the contemporary music industry and other
creative industries,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_01ebaa5c-d2be-4c38-a674-76266c1548e7" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to provide advice to the Minister about other
issues relating to the planning, development, integration or implementation of
policies and programs in the contemporary music industry,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3aa09302-0c03-4f08-905f-ea35ee04f415" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">other functions given to the Board under this Act
or another Act, including in a charter.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5f641b57-e25a-4a4a-b0ff-8e6f3572476a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_093080d3-1bb4-45aa-a6aa-bdb1e9e3773e"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Minister may issue charter</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister may issue a charter to the Board
that provides for&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b78ab36e-df30-4558-a11c-431c02379328" id="sec.8-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">additional functions of the Board,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b5159e95-2ef1-4246-b424-082eb8d8e379" id="sec.8-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the manner in which the Board must
operate.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_982ba839-9adb-4faf-9690-72d77dc6a1d5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_6d80be3f-45de-4654-99f6-584cc040c855"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_33d44b9e-eeff-449f-b5be-8f9fec588d1c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_d7ec2d87-b29e-4e1c-a150-0b0065533a98"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations about a matter
that is&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4993effb-d4ca-43e6-bbf7-6b616d3ec19a" id="sec.9-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">required or permitted by this Act to be
prescribed, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_349d8525-4562-4fbf-a534-2cad2f507d29" id="sec.9-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">necessary or convenient to be prescribed for
carrying out or giving effect to this Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_61905c7a-dd0b-4698-81af-05b19a2d8782"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_e0515ac8-1ede-429a-9948-4736500584a6"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Review of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_934ab099-84f7-4190-b944-5fb4eeee9503"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister must review the operation of section
6(2) and regulations made under section 6(2) to determine whether the
composition of the Board remains appropriate for&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6fb46483-9665-4aa6-b817-1ce6717bbead" id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">representing the contemporary music industry in
New South Wales, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_5114e5f1-64c1-459d-8cbd-75223b7fc194" id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">otherwise achieving the policy objectives of this
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bf6072f8-3f14-4c8b-b3f3-34cb20733996"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The review must be undertaken as soon as possible
after the period of 3 years from the commencement of this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6cab2024-1eed-4fd3-a191-c8f04db90b39"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A report on the outcome of the review must be
tabled in each House of Parliament as soon as practicable after the end of the
period of 3 years.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


